        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Fibo 2.0 Dev with LoRAs\n\n**Dev** is the non-distilled Fibo 2.0 checkpoint that LoRAs and fine-tunes target (Bria ships a single-GPU LoRA trainer\nin the Dev repo). No LoRA is required: Dev runs as it is.\n\n**Settings**: 50 steps (30 is faster), CFG 5 (true CFG), euler, simple, 1248×832 (about 1 MP, sides multiples of 16).\nNo shift setting. Leave the negative prompt empty (the trained null caption) or use the `NEGATIVE_T2I` JSON of the\nDev model card.\n\n**Prompts**: plain sentences or a VGL JSON caption (`short_description`, `objects` with one entry per\nperson or item, `background_setting`, `lighting`, `photographic_characteristics`, `style_medium`,\n`text_render`), pasted into the prompt. Strings to render go into `text_render` (or quotes in plain\nprompts). No booru tags, no quality tokens, `(word:1.2)` weights do not work. The prompt here is a VGL caption; VGL with one object per person fixes the miscounted groups of\nplain prompts.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:pp` | Image Bench Prompt | prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:np` | Text Encode Fibo 2 | negative prompt (its `negative_prompt` widget) |\n| `ib:smp` | KSampler | seed, steps, CFG scale, sampling method, schedule type; size (Width / Height) |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list of the Generate tab, or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt; the **Image\nBench Prompt** node applies them. **Load LoRA** stays bypassed; LoRA exploration enables it for its runs and bypasses\nit again.\n\nThe size goes through **Width** / **Height** into Text Encode Fibo 2, whose `latent` output is the empty latent.\n\nFibo 2.0 needs a ComfyUI with the **TextEncodeFibo2** node (master after 21 Oct 2026, PR #17240; v0.42.3\nand older lack it). The CLIP loader type must be `fibo2`.\n\n## Model Links\n\n[Comfy-Org/Fibo-2.0](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Fibo-2.0) (ungated repack of [briaai/Fibo-2.0-dev](https://huggingface.co/briaai/Fibo-2.0-dev) and\n[briaai/Fibo-2.0-edit-turbo](https://huggingface.co/briaai/Fibo-2.0-edit-turbo)) also has the `*_bf16` diffusion models (16.45 GB) and the\n`qwen3vl_4b_int8_convrot` text encoder (text-to-image only: it errors on image input).\n\n**diffusion_models**: [fibo2_dev_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Fibo-2.0/resolve/main/diffusion_models/fibo2_dev_int8_convrot.safetensors), [fibo2_edit_turbo_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Fibo-2.0/resolve/main/diffusion_models/fibo2_edit_turbo_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Fibo-2.0/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors) (one file for Dev and Edit Turbo)\n**vae**: [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Fibo-2.0/resolve/main/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors) (the FLUX.2 VAE)\n\nFibo 2.0 is released under CC BY-NC 4.0 (non-commercial; commercial use needs an agreement with Bria).\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: Fibo 2.0 Dev with LoRAs",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
